Subject: [PATCH 478/488] [DS4.1] SP exchange and rank-order all-reduce: pad
 rows are not filled

Prefill SP's unreduced exchange zero-filled the pad rows of the last rank's
block (two BF16 fills a layer when the token count is not a multiple of the TP
size), and the rank-order all-reduce zero-padded its buffer. Neither value
reaches a real row: every op on SP local rows is row-wise and every gather
keeps the first T rows, and the all-reduce drops its padding rows after the
gather. The fills are gone; the documented invariant now says pad rows are
arbitrary after unreduced parts.

The tests poison or refuse the fills and check the real rows bit for bit.
